{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/81415-sidereal-and-fey-rules-and-possibilities","id":81415,"title":"Sidereal and Fey - Rules and possibilities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-27T21:49:03-08:00","id":81415,"title":"Sidereal and Fey - Rules and possibilities","content":"Right now I'm running a gDocs game where one of my players is a raksha, and a Sidereal's presence is coming due. I only barely understand some of the raksha rules, and am spotty on Sidereals too, so I'm attempting to troubleshoot ambiguities, only to find more in the process.<br /> <br /> A) <span style=\"font-size:13px\">In what circumstances can a Sidereal's Resplendent Destiny be rendered invisible/inactive? </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">My raksha player carries two.. uh.. items... that confer(?) the power of Mad God Mien(GWM pg 160). Presumably that means that as long as the character 'holds' the things, he's considered outside of fate. But I'm not even sure whether that means he does not see a Sidereal's resplendent destiny. And what about other entities - Demons, Abyssals, Infernals?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">B) Emerald or Sapphire Countermagic can render some raksha stuff temporarily inert. Or destroyed, barring the inclusion of Mad God Mien. What are the categories of stuff countermagic affects? Or doesn't affect?</span><br /> Are the affected categories Oneiromancies? Adjurations? Behemoths? Treasures? Any/all? And what's the difference between those labels, anyways? Seems like fluff. They all just seem like items. My player's character sheet has some items listed under a category of &quot;Dreams,&quot; which I don't think is an official term, so now I'm unsure whats what. A scarf and a mask that appears to confer charms. What categories might these be accurately called, and what differentiates it from the other confusing crap in GWM?<br /> <br /> C) Can these varied raksha items be transferred to others, to confer benefit? If I decided that an NPC had a history with a raksha(NPC or PC), could it be possible that the non-raksha took posession or ownership or ... whatever... of any given [insert raksha buzzword]? Therefore allowing a non-raksha access to raksha power? It seems oaths need to be acquired from someone/something else before getting .. er, empowered or whatever. So concievably someone could steal my players oath? An exalt perhaps? And what about the scarf, or mask? Or beyond these, are there any limitations as to what a mortal(for example) could gainfully take from a raksha?<br /> <br /> Ugh, this stuff is definitely not so convoluted as 1E(as much as I admire R.S.B.'s creative mind, yikes). But it still seems a bit excessive and confusing.<br /> Any help on the subject, broadly, would be beneficial. Thanks all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2401-mok","name":"MOK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T22:30:17-08:00","id":81428,"title":"","content":"A) Resplendent Destinies cannot be seen by beings which are Outside of Fate! This includes-<br /> <br /> - Raksha with Mad God Mien<br /> - Infernals<br /> - Demons of the Second Circle and higher, depending<br /> <br /> But does not include Abyssals, who are Inside Fate by default.<br /> <br /> <br /> Alas, I don't know the other answers! Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T00:31:09-08:00","id":81455,"title":"","content":"I think other people can use raksha items, I have heard of a solar using a staff grace he got from a fair folk. But I don't know the details of it and the guy was raised as a fair folk slave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T01:26:51-08:00","id":81468,"title":"","content":"Behemoths are, essentially, mortal creatures that you stack mutations on top of. So you take a common wolf, you stack the Huge mutation on it a couple of times, then you stack two Extra Head mutations. You give it the Breath Weapon mutation. You got yourself a fire breathing Cerberus. Pretty straight forward.<br /> <br /> Adjurations are a way to add Mutations onto yourself. You make an oath and in exchange you get certain mutations. In Creation, an Adjuration doesn't really exist and doesn't have a form; just like real oaths, it's an ephemeral concept (though in the Wyld they are &quot;things&quot; that can be taken from other people). Again, fairly straight forward.<br /> <br /> Oneiromancy are magical spells. These are vulnerable to Countermagic. Essentially they tend to produce long lasting effects. Basically think of them as granting the character bonus Charms, which tend to be limited in how you can use them (for example the Paupers Mask allows the owner to cast Hateful Coin Curse, but only against people who see the mask). You build them using Mutation Points to grant the spell both charms (effects) and vectors which allow you to affect people with those charms.<br /> <br /> Finally you have Treasures, which are a bit more like standard Creation Artifacts, each with their own powers and abilities.<br /> <br /> Regardless, you can give Behemoths, Adjurations, Oneiromancies and Treasures to other people. They still have to attune to them to be able to use them. Many of these tend to be fairly expensive to attune to, and Raksha have fairly small mote pools. So it's common for a Raksha lord to give some of his stuff out to his servants and have them attune to those for him. So a Raksha lord might have a Stablemaster who attunes to his Behemoths or a Vizier who attunes to his Oneiromancies, When the Raksha needs to summon forth his Cerberus, he summons up his Stablemaster who then summons Cerberus.<br /> <br /> Your players Scarf and Mask (which provide Charms) are probably Oneiromancies.<br /> <br /> And yes, Fair Folk Oneiromancies, Treasures and Behemoths can be given to or stolen by other people, including the Creationborn (Adjurations can be stolen too, but as they don't have a physical form in Creation, they can usually only be stolen in the Wyld).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T01:44:54-08:00","id":81474,"title":"","content":"A) Just as the Mercury says, although I'd point out that just because the Raksha isn't effected doesn't mean the Destiny is inert. Other characters will still interact with the Sidereal as though he were his assumed identity, Resplendancy powers are still available to him, and so forth. <br /> <br /> (As an aside, I'm not a Raksha expert but I'm struggling to see what those items would be. The usual means used to bestow long-term Charm effects are Oaths, but they only bestow mutations and by my reading Mad God Mein isn't eligible. They could be Treasures but a Treasure that just replicates a Charm is uninspired, to say the least, and carry two would be fairly odd. Could be worth touching base with your player and finding out just what he sees these being.)<br /> <br /> B) Only Oneriomancies are effected by countermagic.<br /> <br /> The different categories of Raksha Artifacts vary in a few key ways, their composition, their Shaping function, and their effect in Creation. <br /> <br /> Every Wyld Artifact is made from a Grace, and each type of Grace can only be made into it's associated artifact. You can't take a Sword Grace and make a Treasure, for example, or forge a Ring grace into a Behemoth. Likewise each artifact only helps in it's associated type of Shaping combat. A Behemoth is a powerful tool for Sword Shaping, but useless for Staff Shaping. <br /> <br /> Treasures (Ring) are the most straightforward. Anything that might be an artifact for an Exalt could be a treasure. A Noble's glass sword or spiderweb armor would be Treasures, possibly also your scarf and mask (though I wouldn't really be a fan of a player taking two artifacts that just replicate the same Charm).<br /> <br /> Oaths, also called Abdjurations, (Staff) grant bonuses over the long term in the form of mutation points, which can be taken either as Wyld mutations or certain types of Raksha Charms that are eligible to be taken as mutations. In Creation they tend to manifest as intangibles, lights, sounds and will-o-the-whisps.<br /> <br /> Behemoths (Sword) are monsters and Wyld creatures, a sort of Rakhsa answer to Familiars if you take into account that Behemoths can get massive and dangerous and familiars generally ... don't. Uniquely among Raksha Artifacts, Behemoths can be slain by the Creation-Born. <br /> <br /> Oneriomancies (Cup) are the Raksha Equivalent to Sorcery. The are the Raksha's primary means of using reality-shaping on others in Creation, since free form shaping is prohibitively difficult there and also a means of imposing effects over a wide area with spells build around Assumption of the (Land's/City's) Heart. Oneriomancies can include Mad God Mein (so your mask and scarf could fall here) but in this case they wouldn't confer the power of that Charm on the Raksha character. <br /> <br /> C) Yes, non-Raksha can steal or be given all of these items, and can use them in some circumstances. Anyone who can attune an atrifact can use a Treasure. Anyone who bears a Grace (usually meaning they've had the various Forging the [Grace] Grace Charms performed on the by a Raksha) can swear to an Oath or bond to a Behemoth. Only characters who possess gossamer can wield Oneriomancy spells. Any suitably daring Creation-Born can steal a Raksha artifact and just hold onto it, to deny its former owner it's use.<br /> <br /> Hope all that helps!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T02:20:36-08:00","id":81481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/81415-sidereal-and-fey-rules-and-possibilities?p=81428#post81428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A) Resplendent Destinies cannot be seen by beings which are Outside of Fate! This includes-<br /> <br /> - Raksha with Mad God Mien<br /> - Infernals<br /> - Demons of the Second Circle and higher, depending<br /> <br /> But does not include Abyssals, who are Inside Fate by default.<br /> <br /> <br /> Alas, I don't know the other answers! Sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've looked through MoEP: Sidereals, and couldn't find it one way or the other <i>(Perhaps I didn't look hard enough...)</i>, so I always thought that beings &quot;Outside of Fate&quot; couldn't see through Resplendent Destinies, and then I found this......I'll put it in a &quot;Spoiler&quot; for those who don't have &quot;Return of the Scarlet Empress&quot;:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> RotSE, page 40:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>&quot;Mnemon bursts into the Heptagram with a strike force of hundreds of bound demon bodyguards, tearing open the academy\u2019s front gate by the hands of Octavian and Iyutha (or other suitably martial demons selected by the Storyteller). The students and teachers make ready to defend their school, but she calls for peace and has her </i></span><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>Second Circle demon slaves identify the Sidereals hidden among the staff via their innate immunity to resplendent destiny disguises.</i></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>&quot;</i></span></div> <br /> Is there any other place that mentions this, besides RotSE???<br /> <br /> Thanks<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Peace.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T03:01:00-08:00","id":81488,"title":"","content":"A few suggestions on how OP's sid can tangle with said Raksha:<br /> <br /> 1) Sids have a charm that allows them to tie in things outside of fate, into fate. What's a raksha gonna do if he suddenly finds himself bound by icy grip of permanence and causality? Oh dear<br /> <br /> 2) Why is the sid comming after him? Is he making trouble? Eating people's souls? Being naughty? Sids are busy people, will the sid have time to handle all this?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T03:09:55-08:00","id":81490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nadrakas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/81415-sidereal-and-fey-rules-and-possibilities?p=81481#post81481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any other place that mentions this, besides RotSE???</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot resist an invitation to annotate!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoeP:Sidereals, pg 191</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Viziers cannot force destinies upon creatures beyond the reach of fate; they see through the false identities created by Sidereal astrology, and ignore the powers conferred by those guises.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T05:52:18-08:00","id":81536,"title":"","content":"I actually find that it's a little bit unclear how beings outside of Fate interact with the falsities of Arcane Fate and resplendent destinies.<br /> <br /> Like, does immunity to the Arcane Fate also mean that normal difficulties retroactively apply when they encounter a disguised Sidereal, and they lose whatever benefits of the dice bonus? If a Third Circle Demon looks at a Sidereal relying on Arcane Fate to keep people from seeing past their rough persona, does the demon see somebody wearing a really poor makeup job?<br /> <br /> There sometimes seem to be places that assume that the resplendent destiny itself alters your appearance...<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, does getting five successes on a difficulty 1 action qualify the same as succeeding at a difficulty 5 action? Or is a difficulty 1 action assumed to be generally unimpressive regardless of how good your dice roll is? Is the difficulty 1 Arcane Fate aided disguise roll a pretty shoddy disguise regardless of successes, so that somebody unimpeded by the Arcane Fate will definitely see that it's a poor disguise?<br /> <br /> I mean, okay, so a demon won't get that same intrinsic impression of, say, being a stoic labourer for wearing a destiny of the Mast, but if you're still dressed in the manner of a labourer, well, you'll still look like one to them, won't you? Sure, there are probably people who learn to recognise that everybody else is treating the character as though they're an archetypal stoic labourer, and can infer from there, but without that, well.... seeing through resplendent destinies and the Arcane Fate means you see the Sidereal, but unless they're doing something obvious or you're using particular examination powers, that just means they look like a regular person.<br /> <br /> Hmm, now I'm thinking that a key part of the induction course for Sidereals is being taught how to not give themselves away by acting in a surprised manner when somebody actually sees and interacts with them properly, rather than as a vague blur or an astrological archetype.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T06:44:52-08:00","id":81563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/81415-sidereal-and-fey-rules-and-possibilities?p=81488#post81488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Sids have a charm that allows them to tie in things outside of fate, into fate. What's a raksha gonna do if he suddenly finds himself bound by icy grip of permanence and causality? Oh dear</div> </div> </div> </div>Was scanning through my books to check for this interaction -- felt kinda fishy to negate a character's Charm purchase like that. I would have expected at least a roll-off, but no, Mad-God Mien indeed does nothing to protect against effects that drag a raksha back inside fate, though it still keeps the protection against Creation-born shaping:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scroll of Errata, p. 111</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mad God Mien<br /> (pp. 160-161)<br /> Keywords: Glamour (1), Shaped-only<br /> Replace the text of the Charm with the following:<br /> This Charm blurs the line between Creation and the Wyld, between reality and dream. Mad God Mien inflicts a -1 external penalty on all attempts by the Creation-born to use Shaping effects upon the raksha, not including shaping actions produced by the Graces. The raksha is also considered a being outside of fate, although this Charm fails in the face of Charms or other magic designed to force beings outside of fate back within its confines.<br /> Oneiromancy Benefit: Spells with this Charm incorporated into them are immune to destruction by countermagic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, I have no idea how the character is getting the benefits of Mad-God Mien without actually learning the Charm. Sudden Thunder's suggestion of Treasures that do it is probably the best explanation, but still isn't a great one. Treasures are, for all intents and purposes 9 times out of 10, just regular Artifacts; if it's reasonable to have an Artifact grant the Charm's effect (I sincerely have no clue), then it's okay, otherwise it's not. The Gossamer keyword means Adjurations and Behemoths can't have the Charm added, and even Oneiromancies only have the described countermagic protection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T07:01:56-08:00","id":81573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/81415-sidereal-and-fey-rules-and-possibilities?p=81563#post81563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I have no idea how the character is getting the benefits of Mad-God Mien without actually learning the Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Adjoration can do it, as it would grant your charm as a Mutation. Other than that, maybe an artifact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T07:28:26-08:00","id":81583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/81415-sidereal-and-fey-rules-and-possibilities?p=81573#post81573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Adjoration can do it, as it would grant your charm as a Mutation. Other than that, maybe an artifact?</div> </div> </div> </div>An Abjuration couldn't do it, since Mad God Mien has no gossamer cost and cannot be taken as a mutation. The more I think about it the more there seem to be only two options. <br /> <br /> 1) The artifacts in question are onerionmacies in which Mad God Mein applies to the atrifact rather than the Raksha. This is not just OK, it reflects good planning on the part of a Raksha reinforcing her resources for the hostile environment of Creation. <br /> <br /> 2) The artifacts are cheap Treasures or illegal Oaths and the player is trying to have one over on the ST. <br /> <br /> \u200bIn either case the first course of action should be for the ST to speak with the player and get a clearer idea of what the concept for the artifacts is and what category they should fall under. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T07:38:59-08:00","id":81589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/81415-sidereal-and-fey-rules-and-possibilities?p=81573#post81573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Adjoration can do it, as it would grant your charm as a Mutation. Other than that, maybe an artifact?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Sudden Thunder points out, an Adjuration can't: as of the errata, only Charms with the Mutation keyword can be put in an Oath, not those with only the Gossamer keyword. I'm now away from my books and can't check, but perhaps that restriction wasn't in place pre-Errata?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Abjuration and adjuration are not the same. 02-28-2014, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T07:56:59-08:00","id":81595,"title":"","content":"Regarding how he could have a charm within onieromancy, despite not knowing the charm - well, it wouldn't be the first time the player has overlooked details such as that. Frankly that part doesn't bother me, though. <br /> Regarding the Sidereal's purpose, as it relates to lil innocent raksha-dude, that's already accounted for: Vizier is not there for him. Still gonna have to concoct a scheme to un-K.O.S. the raksha, though. I hear Sidereals are, comparatively, less fond of the fair folk. But I think I've got something solid in mind there. <br /> Regarding how a resplendent destiny 'looks' from the outside, I'd read yesterday in the Sidereals book that fellow viziers simply cannot see the R.D. of their peers at all. I would tend to assume that their inability to see them comes from a similar premise as beings outside of fate, and that it's a full-fledged illusion. So the heroic, male, muscular, armorclad, scowling drill sergeant appears instead as Celestial Lady Gaga, or something arbitrarily unrelated, no makeup or props needed(not even for Gaga), no humorous attempt at disguise, no embarrassment, etc.<br /> <br /> So to clarify.... Anything considered outside of fate cannot see a resplendent destiny? Boy, that's a lot of stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding the rationale of differentiation between the prior listed categories, I see the basic premise that each is derived from a particular attribute. Though, they still feel slightly arbitrary - If I can countermagic Cup magic, why should I not be able to countermagic Staff magic, Sword magic? <br /> But that's a minor quibble, more like a semantics argument, easily ignorable.<br /> <br /> Had some other point but I forgot. <br /> Anyways, thank you everyone for your input. It's been very helpful.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2401-mok","name":"MOK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T08:45:32-08:00","id":81609,"title":"","content":"Glad that was a help.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MOK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/81415-sidereal-and-fey-rules-and-possibilities?p=81595#post81595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the rationale of differentiation between the prior listed categories, I see the basic premise that each is derived from a particular attribute. Though, they still feel slightly arbitrary - If I can countermagic Cup magic, why should I not be able to countermagic Staff magic, Sword magic?<br /> But that's a minor quibble, more like a semantics argument, easily ignorable.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might help to remember that they all actually are artifacts. Weird artifacts, but artifacts. Indeed, Treasures are functionally Artifacts by another name.<br /> <br /> Countermagicking away a raksha's attuned giant monster Behemoth (made from a Sword Grace) would be analogous to countermagicking away someone's daiklave.<br /> <br /> Adjurations are more internalized. I can't check my books, but I recall they mostly give mutations, and Permanent Charms that are treated as mutations, to one who swears the Oath. Maybe think of them as working actual, lasting (albeit conditional) changes on the one who swears them.<br /> <br /> Oneiromancies create external and active magic in the world under preset conditions, so they're vulnerable to countermagic. Also analogous to Sorcery spells, Oneiromancies require some time (albeit in scenes) and effort (ill-defined, other than the mote cost to cast them, which comes on top of the attunement cost) to get them going. The other Grace artifacts are good to go the instant one has them attuned (other than swearing the Oath, in the case of an Adjuration).<br /> <br /> Let me know if that helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Abjuration and adjuration are not the same. 02-28-2014, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T09:12:54-08:00","id":81619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MOK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/81415-sidereal-and-fey-rules-and-possibilities?p=81595#post81595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding how he could have a charm within onieromancy, despite not knowing the charm - well, it wouldn't be the first time the player has overlooked details such as that. Frankly that part doesn't bother me, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I can see this is not an issue. A raksha doesn't need to know a particular Charm to have crafted a similar Oneriomancy or vexed one from some other foe somewhere along the line. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MOK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/81415-sidereal-and-fey-rules-and-possibilities?p=81595#post81595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hear Sidereals are, comparatively, less fond of the fair folk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals are not great fans of anyone from beyond the borders of Creation, be they outside fate or not. One imagines there's a circle of neophyte Sidereals watching newly-integrated Autochtonian mortals and just waiting to erupt into a 'no-one-told-us-there-would-be-a-Solar' chronicle. That said the Sidereals do broker 'asylum' deals and there are Raksha within Creation who are tolerated as long as they stay within the guidelines imposed on them. Such deals are tensely watched by both sides, perhaps having the Sidereal appear as the Raksha's 'parole officer' would be an opportunity for storytelling and character development. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MOK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/81415-sidereal-and-fey-rules-and-possibilities?p=81595#post81595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding how a resplendent destiny 'looks' from the outside ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone within fate (suffering the -3 dice to their awareness rolls) sees what fate tells them to see. If Sidereal Chris Hemsworth has a resplendent destiny as tiny, pregnant Natalie Portman then they see a slim, gravid woman. Beings outside of fate see whatever their roll without the penalty dictates. In this instance it really depends on how much effort the Sidereal has put into his guise ... the separation between high-Stealth and low-Stealth Sidereals being their ability to conceal themselves from targets who see through their Resplendant Destinies. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MOK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/81415-sidereal-and-fey-rules-and-possibilities?p=81595#post81595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the rationale of differentiation between the prior listed categories, I see the basic premise that each is derived from a particular attribute. Though, they still feel slightly arbitrary - If I can countermagic Cup magic, why should I not be able to countermagic Staff magic, Sword magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why can you not countermagic an artefact? Or a Charm? Or a familiar? Because countermagic opposes Sorcery. Specifically, not all magic in general. It happens that in their practice of forging magic out of Graces the Raksha have happened upon one type of magic that is vulnerable to Creation-born countermagic. They've also happened upon one form of magic that is vulnerable to stabbing, it doesn't follow that all Ring or Staff artifacts can be killed any more than all Manses or Past Lives can be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T10:52:08-08:00","id":81669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/81415-sidereal-and-fey-rules-and-possibilities?p=81619#post81619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Sidereal Chris Hemsworth has a resplendent destiny as tiny, pregnant Natalie Portman then they see a slim, gravid woman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if he actually disguises himself as such. Arcane Fate helps it to be trivially easy to disguise oneself as implausible things, but you still have to do it; if you don't disguise yourself for any resplendent destinies, people can figure out that multiple apparently different people look exactly the same.<br /> <br /> Or at least, that was how First Edition portrayed it. The Second Edition write-up seems to have dropped most of the details and instead goes for the much more vague &quot;you get a +3 bonus to convince them of the validity of your identity, even if it's grossly inappropriate to appearance, mannerisms or biology&quot;. So apparently, a resplendent destiny of a pregnant woman is readily convincing even if somebody is looking right at you and can note that you have no bump and also a penis.<br /> <br /> Wait, what the fuck? So you gain a bonus to make the destiny's identity convincing even if it doesn't line up with appearance or mannerisms, but acting out of character with the identity you've set up still provokes Paradox? That's not a mixed message at all.<br /> <br /> Jesus that book was awful.<br /> <br /> Note that, in First Edition, the penalties and bonuses applied to the Sidereal's attempts to bullshit their way out of being recognised. It was like in Aladdin, when Jasmine points out that Al totally looks the same as a prince that he did as a street urchin, and he claims that he likes to occasionally dress up as a poor person. You still look the same, but nobody thinks too hard about it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T11:12:05-08:00","id":81679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/81415-sidereal-and-fey-rules-and-possibilities?p=81490#post81490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I cannot resist an invitation to annotate!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I don't play with too many Sidereal PCs <i>(Been a while)</i> and they end up being &quot;behind the scene&quot; NPCs in my game.<br /> <br /> Thanks again.<br /> <br /> <i>(BTW: I'd rather have a reference and page number any day....so annotation is appreciated...)</i><br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T11:15:18-08:00","id":81683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/81415-sidereal-and-fey-rules-and-possibilities?p=81669#post81669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only if he actually disguises himself as such. Arcane Fate helps it to be trivially easy to disguise oneself as implausible things, but you still have to do it; if you don't disguise yourself for any resplendent destinies, people can figure out that multiple apparently different people look exactly the same.<br /> <br /> Or at least, that was how First Edition portrayed it. The Second Edition write-up seems to have dropped most of the details and instead goes for the much more vague &quot;you get a +3 bonus to convince them of the validity of your identity, even if it's grossly inappropriate to appearance, mannerisms or biology&quot;. So apparently, a resplendent destiny of a pregnant woman is readily convincing even if somebody is looking right at you and can note that you have no bump and also a penis.<br /> <br /> Wait, what the fuck? So you gain a bonus to make the destiny's identity convincing even if it doesn't line up with appearance or mannerisms, but acting out of character with the identity you've set up still provokes Paradox? That's not a mixed message at all.<br /> <br /> Jesus that book was awful.<br /> <br /> Note that, in First Edition, the penalties and bonuses applied to the Sidereal's attempts to bullshit their way out of being recognised. It was like in Aladdin, when Jasmine points out that Al totally looks the same as a prince that he did as a street urchin, and he claims that he likes to occasionally dress up as a poor person. You still look the same, but nobody thinks too hard about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fairly sure that in 2E the &quot;Arcane Fate&quot; and &quot;Resplendent Destiny&quot; rules are entirely unconnected. The former gives you easy access to disguises, possibly regardless of circumstance. The latter gives you a super-convincing illusion as long as you pay attention to a couple of the listed trappings--but beings outside of fate are immune to the illusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T11:28:11-08:00","id":81691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/81415-sidereal-and-fey-rules-and-possibilities?p=81669#post81669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if he actually disguises himself as such. Arcane Fate helps it to be trivially easy to disguise oneself as implausible things, but you still have to do it, but nobody thinks too hard about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but 'disguise' in this sense might be awfully broad. Chris can shove a pillow under his shirt, or hand write a sign that says 'Natalie Portman' and potentially get away with it. Making the absolute minimum effort possible a Sidereal has a six-dice advantage on their observer. An unskilled and unprepared Sidereal can crush an exceptional mortal observer. With a bit of skill at disguise he can beat all comers. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T12:03:08-08:00","id":81712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/81415-sidereal-and-fey-rules-and-possibilities?p=81691#post81691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but 'disguise' in this sense might be awfully broad.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no &quot;might be&quot; about it; hence &quot;trivially easy to disguise oneself as implausible things&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fairly sure that in 2E the &quot;Arcane Fate&quot; and &quot;Resplendent Destiny&quot; rules are entirely unconnected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit I'm not quite sure, since it would seem that the Second Edition take is in no way as interesting or memorable as in the original book.<br /> <br /> Like, the idea that Arcane Fate makes you nondescript enough to ride along with the archetypal impressions given off by a resplendent destiny to craft a memorable alternate persona, that's unconventional and synergistic in a way that is distinctly Sidereal. Resplendent destinies as just another generic illusion power sucks my interest right out of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T12:21:03-08:00","id":81723,"title":"","content":"RE: RDs and Arcane Fate<br /> <br /> You're right that RDs are not terribly specific. They don't specify the creation of any illusion effect, but the text of the segment says that people '<i>see only the false identity</i>'. My refuge has always been back to the 1e logic of Sidereal charms which involved Fate, like Avoidance Kata. It's not that you don't see that the pregnant woman is actually a guy with a pillow stuffed under his shirt, it's just that your eyes are getting outvoted by how <i>obviously</i> he's a pregnant woman. You can feel that with a total certainty! <br /> <br /> (This also fits with the trend of using those as disguises since the Breaking of the Mask. Arcane Fate makes the actual Sidereal difficult to spot, or focus on, or even remember. Resplendent Destinies give a very powerful impression of a specific sort of person, so it's very easy to just go with that instead.)<br /> <br /> ...but that's not actually <i>spelled out</i>. I just think that's the best interpretation of the mechanics which exist.<br /> <br /> And this does mean that someone Outside Fate will look at the Sidereal and see a guy with a pillow stuffed up his shirt. If the Sidereal's bothered with a good disguise, they might not notice anything wrong at all, although a properly paranoid Sidereal might leave a small-but-explicable inconsistency just to identify people who point it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}